e Act with the stroke of a  pen because he has that capacity is the  President of the United States even  without Congress Congress could  undermine the Affordable Care Act every  single year if they had authorized these  CSR payments but they didn't so  President Obama back in 2014  took it into his own hands and used the  executive branch to authorize these  payments from the Treasury  well this presupposes that you are going  to always have somebody in power that is  actually a decent human being right  Obamacare required  that you either have a House of  Representatives and a Senate and a  president for that matter to sign off on  the budget but to at least have a House  of Representatives that were willing to  sign off on these CSR payments annually  as a part of their budget and we haven't  had that since the Democrat Republicans  took over in 2010 I believe 2010 was the  year that the Republicans got the  majority in the house  so Obamacare required and necessitated  to have decent people who cared about  health care for all in the House of  Representatives or at a minimum in the  White House and without having somebody  decent in the White House we now see  that Obamacare is uniquely vulnerable  because we have a president who has the  ability to sign away a system that is  going to fundamentally destabilize Obama  care all right so there's a lot more to  cover on this issue and we'll definitely  keep our eyes on it but I think it's  very important for us to see these these  fundamental flaws in Obamacare not as a  way of criticizing what President Obama  did or what Nancy Pelosi did or what all  the other people who did they put a lot  of time into building it but now we see  it's very exposed how detrimental or how  vulnerable rather this program is to the  whims of a narcissistic president and  because of that I think it's vitally  important that we begin to advocate for  the same thing that Kamala Harris is  advocating for the same thing that  Elizabeth 